ia's girls  to get on a roll  welcome back in nova scotia a growing  number of women and girls  are rolling into a new sport an  all-girls skate crew is now leading a  skateboarding tour for women throughout  the province this weekend  it's all part of a wider effort to  encourage women on wheels  to take on a sport traditionally  dominated by men  alexa mclean has more  i've got it i'm poppy george i'm 10  years old and we're at halifax skate  park right now  when poppy was first introduced to  skateboarding by her father  she had no idea she would be joining the  ranks  of a fast-growing movement of girls and  women in nova scotia  getting involved in this traditionally  male-dominated sport  we do this for girls to encourage girls  but we want to include  everyone that's transgender non-binary  all the guys we love the guys like we  love everyone we just want to see  everyone get together and have a really  good time  and give girls the motivation to come  out and actually try this sport they  might be  too intimidated to do otherwise katie  mott is a founding member of a  grassroots group  called skate in the slow lane  a self-proclaimed girl skate crew  originating on the south shore of the  province  during the early days of the pandemic  the crew gained a lot of online  attention through videos they posted now  that restrictions have loosened the  crews are leading a tour  throughout different skate parks in the  province with covet protocols in place  it's super motivating constant progress  everyone just feeds off each other's  energy  it's not a competition at all for poppy  having these young women as role models  helps foster her sense  of self confidence be yourself and do  what you want to do  and it's just super exciting to know  that i'm not the only girl who  skateboards  the crew is now focused on growing the  community by empowering girls and women  to take on the sport  hoping that growth will help everyone  through an unprecedented time  people are a lot more accepting than  you'd think if you just go out there  with a good attitude  and try things and we are always always  always into having new people show up  and skate with us  alexa mclean global news halifax and  that is global national for this sunday  i'm jeff semple tonight your canada  is this lovely shot of a crab fishing  boat being welcomed home to cartwright  on the coast of labrador  thanks for watching have a great night  you
 

